From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:46:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 031/342] dwc2: let slow devices NAK bulk transfers for as long
 as they need

A host channel that had not halted within 2 s was halted and the
transfer failed with "no response". In DMA mode the core retries NAKed
bulk and control transactions by itself, so a device that NAKs for more
than 2 s lost its transfer, mid-way, with the data toggle out of step;
the mass storage reset that followed failed the same way. A Verbatim
STORE N GO stick takes up to 16 s to accept writes while it programs
its flash: BFS's first write after mounting failed and the volume could
not be unmounted again.

Bulk transfers now run until they complete or are canceled (usb_disk
cancels after 10 s), control transfers get the 5 s USB 2.0 limit, and
interrupt transfers, which halt on a NAK, keep 2 s. A cancel no longer
logs "no response".

Tested on the ODROID-C2 with that stick: 8 x 32 MB raw writes (the
first took 16 s) read back identical; hot-plugged volume unmounted;
mkfs, copies, unmount, remount and verify; no USB errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp | 39 +++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp
index a37ede7fe8..f9eaf38422 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/dwc2.cpp
@@ -1081,11 +1081,34 @@ DWC2::_RunChannel(dwc2_lane* lane, uint32 character, uint32 split,
 	asm volatile("dsb sy" : : : "memory");
 	_Write(HC_CHAR(lane->channel), character | HCCHAR_CHENA);
 
-	entry.Wait(B_RELATIVE_TIMEOUT, 2000000);
-	uint32 status = atomic_get(&lane->status);
-	if ((status & HCINT_CHHLTD) == 0) {
-		_HaltChannel(lane);
-		return B_DEV_TIMEOUT;
+	// In DMA mode the core retries NAKed bulk and control transactions by
+	// itself; the channel halts when the transfer is done or fails. A bulk
+	// transfer may be NAKed for seconds (a USB stick writing its flash), so
+	// it runs until it is canceled: the class driver has its own timeout.
+	// Control transfers get the 5 s USB 2.0 limit, the others (interrupt
+	// transfers halt on a NAK) 2 s.
+	uint32 type = (character >> HCCHAR_EPTYPE_SHIFT) & 3;
+	bigtime_t limit = type == EPTYPE_BULK ? 0
+		: type == EPTYPE_CONTROL ? 5000000 : 2000000;
+	bigtime_t start = system_time();
+	uint32 status;
+	while (true) {
+		entry.Wait(B_RELATIVE_TIMEOUT, 100000);
+		status = atomic_get(&lane->status);
+		if ((status & HCINT_CHHLTD) != 0)
+			break;
+		// set by CancelQueuedTransfers() for the transfer this lane runs
+		bool canceled = lane->current != NULL
+			&& *(volatile bool*)&lane->current->canceled;
+		if (canceled || (limit != 0 && system_time() - start >= limit)) {
+			_HaltChannel(lane);
+			return canceled ? B_CANCELED : B_DEV_TIMEOUT;
+		}
+		lane->halted.Add(&entry);
+		// it may have halted before the entry was added again
+		status = atomic_get(&lane->status);
+		if ((status & HCINT_CHHLTD) != 0)
+			break;
 	}
 
 	if (in)
@@ -1138,8 +1161,10 @@ DWC2::_Transaction(dwc2_lane* lane, Pipe* pipe, uint32 pid, bool in,
 	status_t result = _RunChannel(lane, _ChannelCharacteristics(pipe, in, false), 0,
 		size, packets, pid, offset, in, &status, &transferSize);
 	if (result != B_OK) {
-		ERROR("device %d endpoint %d: no response\n", pipe->DeviceAddress(),
-			pipe->EndpointAddress() & 0xf);
+		if (result == B_DEV_TIMEOUT) {
+			ERROR("device %d endpoint %d: no response\n", pipe->DeviceAddress(),
+				pipe->EndpointAddress() & 0xf);
+		}
 		return result;
 	}
 
